{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויאמר בני גד", :translit "vayomer bnei gad", :gloss "And said the sons of Gad"} {:he "ויאמרו", :translit "vayomeru", :gloss "and they said"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Grammatical anomaly: singular verb ויאמר with plural subject בני גד instead of expected plural ויאמרו"}], :frame {:text "After the sons of Gad and Reuben receive Moses' terms, the narrative records their reply in Numbers 32:25 with the singular ויאמר ('and he said') rather than the expected plural ויאמרו ('and they said'), even though multiple tribesmen are involved. Ba'al HaTurim resolves this by explaining that the leader among them spoke on behalf of the entire group.", :sources ["Numbers 32:25"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Grammatical anomaly: singular verb ויאמר with plural subject בני גד instead of expected plural ויאמרו", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:32:23.415577881Z", :model "glm-5.2"}